- action(n1, "start loan application process"): Hallucinates an introductory step; the source explicitly begins with "At the start, the loan application is checked." without any prior actions. (SMC1)
- action(n4, "end process"), action(n6, "end process"), action(n8, "end process"): Incorrectly models termination as discrete activities preceding `end()` nodes, whereas the source describes ending as a direct state transition ("the process ends"). (SMC2)
- guard(b2, n6, v2 = 'No') & precedence(b2, n6): Introduces an explicit termination path for declined special terms that is not documented in the source ("if special terms are agreed upon, the process continues"), constituting hallucinated behavior. (SMC1)

Structural Check
